<article class="env-lemma" id="0DNI">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DNI">Lemma <span data-tag="0DNI">108.9.3</span>.</a> The morphism $\mathrm{Pic}_{X/B} \to B$ is quasi-separated and locally of finite presentation. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      To check $\mathrm{Pic}_{X/B} \to B$ is quasi-separated we have to show that its diagonal is quasi-compact. This is immediate from Lemma <a href="/tag/0DMF" data-tag="0DMF">108.9.2</a>. Since the morphism $\mathcal{P}\! \mathit{ic}_{X/B} \to \mathrm{Pic}_{X/B}$ is surjective, flat, and locally of finite presentation (by Lemma <a href="/tag/0DME" data-tag="0DME">108.9.1</a> and Morphisms of Stacks, Lemma <a href="/tag/06QI" data-tag="06QI">101.28.8</a>) it suffices to prove that $\mathcal{P}\! \mathit{ic}_{X/B} \to B$ is locally of finite presentation, see Morphisms of Stacks, Lemma <a href="/tag/06Q9" data-tag="06Q9">101.27.12</a>. This follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/0DMB" data-tag="0DMB">108.8.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>